  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Jowhar off-stream storage programme governance for adaptation to climate change # Maareynta Isbeddelka Cimilada</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building on the results achieved by UNIDO within the framework of the recently completed Productive Sectors Development Joint Programme for Somalia (SAP ID 190362), UNIDO has been offer the opportunity to join a FAO-led joint programme initiative called #Jowhar Off Stream Programme# (JOSP). JOSP is an area-based development programme targeting the overall revitalization of the Middle Shabelle region in the State of Hirshabelle. The overall objective of JOPS is to restore the functionality and operations of large irrigation scheme in the Middle Shabelle region with a view to substantially reduce flood risk, mitigate drought, support local production, and boost food security for an entire swathe of the country, enhancing climate resilience for approximately 1.65million people.  JOSP is funded is an initiative led by FAO, and implemented with the participation of UNIDO, UNEP, IOM and UN-Habitat. JOSP funding appeal will be finalized during the PA phase. At this stage, in order to segment the fundraising efforts from the various funding streams been identified by FAO, JOSP currently comprises of 3 different JPs and projects: JOSP to with UNIDO is part of, that will be funded by SJF (and UN-PBF); TRANSFORM project (currently funded by USaid to FAO) and RESTORE project (currently funded by FCDO to FAO). The detailed</narrative>
  </description>
